    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Period is divided into the Early Vedic (1500–1000 BCE) and Later Vedic (1000–600 BCE) ages based on literary and archaeological evidence.",
        "The Rigveda is the earliest written record of Indo-Aryan culture, containing 1,028 hymns organized into 10 Mandalas.",
        "Iron technology (Krishna Ayas) emerged during the Later Vedic period, transforming pastoral nomadic society into settled agrarian communities.",
        "Political organization evolved from tribal assemblies (Sabha, Samiti, Vidatha) to territorial monarchies known as Janapadas.",
        "The Upanishads (Vedanta) mark the philosophical culmination of Vedic thought, focusing on the concepts of Atman and Brahman."
      ],
      "id": "jnxzdxt"
    },
